{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED: independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review of exact clean pushed head 3fd75543f80c42b400fdd446e1c5b4524e39e200 on request/decision-records-ui-current, verified in the clean checkout at /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/decision-records-ui-current whose HEAD equals this commit and whose status is clean, answering #11627's two mandated examinations directly. Both examinations CONFIRM the defects codex named; changes-requested is the outcome your request predicted.\n\nARCHITECTURE. Affected layers: the layer 7 surface (ui/) and the layer 5/7 derivation boundary that docs/reference/architecture.md@3fd75543 states for it; kernel and application contracts are unchanged. The head does not preserve its own stated contract, so the page must be corrected in the same head that repairs the code. EXAMINATION (a) ADMISSION-TIME AUTHORITY — CONFIRMED. ui/src/lib/authority.ts:43-49 resolves the satisfier from definitionOf(statement.kind, vocabulary) where vocabulary is the live published set (api.ts:195); internal/workroom/fold.go:617-624 captures target.definition once when the target statement is admitted, and fold.go:955 judges every later ratification by target.definition.Satisfier, i.e. the admission-time value. Kind-definition supersession refreshes the live map (fold.go:515-525, 844-894) without touching already-admitted targets' captured definitions. Constructed divergence: kind K admitted with satisfier role:ratifier; target T of K admitted; K then redefined as originating-requester. T's original requester (holding no ratifier role) is offered Ratify by mayRatify under the live rule, signs, and the fold records INEFFECTIVE \"actor lacks ratifier role\" — a permanent ineffective row created by a button the screen said was authorized, contradicting authority.ts:15-20's own invariant (\"The browser must not offer an act the fold will refuse\"). The reverse evolution hides an act the fold would accept. The client cannot even see the admission-time rule: Statement carries no per-record satisfier (api.ts:14-43), only lifecycle. The existing tests cannot catch this because ratification.test.mjs fixes one unchanging starter vocabulary (test lines 14-22).\n\nSECURITY. Unresolved authority-boundary defect: examination (a) lets the layer 7 surface offer acts the fold refuses, appending durable ineffective records signed by a real key — log pollution and operator deception at the trust boundary between what the screen claims and what the fold enforces. Second, disclosure defect: examination (b) RENDERED CITATION DISCLOSURE — CONFIRMED. Toolbar.tsx routes bases arrays (lines 132, 134, 140, 164, 173, 177, 183, 186); request-review includes the artifact event plus up to CITED_PROPOSAL_LIMIT ratified proposals (Toolbar.tsx:173; records.ts:96-109). The composer renders only the act-type badge, request addressee/conditions fields, textarea and error (Thread.tsx:599-684) and submits rests_on: bases at Thread.tsx:581 without rendering any base identifier. Toolbar.tsx:153-156's comment (\"they are visible in the composer before anything is signed\") and docs/reference/architecture.md (\"The operator reads the citation in the composer before signing\") are therefore contradicted by the code on every routed path beyond the prefill text. Operators sign causal references they were never shown. Tests inspect callback arguments rather than rendered output (decision-records.test.mjs:188), so they cannot see this either.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. No cut requested beyond the repairs; one direction: rather than reimplementing fold authority rules client-side, have the projection expose each statement's admitted-time definition (or a fold-published per-record may-act answer) and let mayRatify read that — it removes the dual-source-of-truth defect class instead of patching over it, and renders the citation list from the same single array the submit path uses.\n\nCONDITIONS OF SATISFACTION ACTUALLY MET, named exactly: gofmt -l clean; go build ./... exit 0; go vet ./... exit 0; go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... ./internal/service/... ok (139.7s + 94.1s); make ui-check exit 0 with git status --porcelain -- internal/service/uidist empty; npm test --prefix ui 94/94 pass (the first run's single failure was spawnSync go ENOENT from the child PATH, reproduced green with Go on PATH); git diff --check clean; worktree clean throughout. NOT RUN: the full go test ./... matrix — the two targeted packages alone took ~234s, putting the suite far outside this cycle's budget, so I do not claim it green. This verdict stands on the two source-level examinations, which are decisive for changes-requested regardless; the full matrix remains a condition for any future approval of the repaired head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:862e8bb52c7dc69ecb07898f7eae2ff6f8efa82b","head":"3fd75543f80c42b400fdd446e1c5b4524e39e200","verdict":"changes-requested"}}